The shop is large and bright.
I go to the summer jackets.
There are so many colours and styles here.
I need a jacket for the Berlin summer.
It must not be too warm.
I find two nice jackets on the clothes rack.
One jacket is dark blue and the other is light green.
I take both jackets from the clothes rack.
First, I look closely at the blue jacket.
It looks very elegant, but the fabric is a bit thick.
Then I look at the green jacket.
The green jacket is a bit longer than the blue jacket.
I like that a lot.
Moreover, it is much lighter than the blue jacket.
The thin fabric is perfect for warm days.
The decision is really easy.
I hang the blue jacket back up.
I contentedly drape the green jacket over my arm.
